All 15 tests pass. Here's the summary of every bug fixed:

### `src/auth.py` — 2 bugs
- **`has_permission`**: did case-sensitive `in` check; now lowercases both sides via a set comprehension (`src/auth.py:10`)
- **`is_admin_or_owner`**: used `and` (user must be both admin AND owner); changed to `or` (`src/auth.py:15`)

### `src/inventory.py` — 4 bugs
- **Mutable default arg**: `initial={}` was shared across all instances, causing `test_two_inventories_do_not_share_state` to fail; now `None` with a fresh copy per call (`src/inventory.py:9`)
- **`add` overwrote instead of accumulated**: `self._stock[sku] = qty` → `self._stock.get(sku, 0) + qty` (`src/inventory.py:16`)
- **`reserve` rejected exactly-available**: `qty >=` → `qty >` so reserving all available stock is legal (`src/inventory.py:24`)
- **`release` could go negative**: no guard; now raises `ValueError` when `qty > current` reserved (`src/inventory.py:33-34`)

### `src/text_utils.py` — 3 bugs
- **`slugify` not lowercasing**: added `.lower()` on alnum chars (`src/text_utils.py:15`)
- **`slugify` producing consecutive separators**: the old `.replace("--", "-")` only collapsed pairs, leaving triple `---` as `--`; rewrote to track last-char state so consecutive separators are never appended (`src/text_utils.py:17-19`)
- **`truncate` didn't subtract suffix length**: `text[:max_len] + suffix` could exceed `max_len`; now slices at `max_len - len(suffix)` (`src/text_utils.py:31`)
